 {id:'fifth',region:['Midtown','Downtown'],title:'Fifth Avenue, top to bottom',subtitle:'Park to square, one long and lovely avenue.',area:'Central Park → Washington Square',minutes:100,miles:'2.7',image:'flatiron',tags:['First-time favorites','Film & TV','Architecture'],stops:['plaza','nypl','flatiron','washington'],description:'Follow Fifth Avenue from the edge of Central Park all the way to where it begins. Four famous faces, one easy-to-follow route, and plenty of places to rest along the way.',legs:['Begin at The Plaza, Fifth Avenue and Central Park South (59th Street).','Walk south on Fifth Avenue to 41st Street. The library is on your right.','Continue south on Fifth Avenue to 23rd Street, where Fifth meets Broadway.','Keep going south on Fifth Avenue until it ends at the arch in Washington Square Park.']},
 {id:'grandtour',region:['Midtown'],title:'Grand entrances',subtitle:'A station, a library, and a famous corner.',area:'Midtown → Flatiron',minutes:60,miles:'1.2',image:'grandcentral',tags:['Architecture','First-time favorites'],stops:['grandcentral','nypl','flatiron'],description:'Three buildings that know how to make an entrance. Start under a painted sky, climb the library steps, and finish where Broadway slices across Fifth Avenue.',legs:['Begin at Grand Central Terminal, 42nd Street and Park Avenue.','Walk west on 42nd Street to Fifth Avenue. The library steps face Fifth Avenue.','Walk south on Fifth Avenue to 23rd Street, where Fifth meets Broadway.']},
 {id:'plottwists',region:['Downtown'],title:'Downtown Plot Twists',subtitle:'Cinema, photography, angels, art, and Hamilton.',area:'Nolita → NoHo',minutes:70,miles:'1.3',image:'bayard',tags:['Film & TV','Hidden gems','Architecture'],stops:['puck','oldcathedral','germania','bayard','basquiat','publictheater'],description:'Six buildings with a surprise behind each façade. Start with a gilded troublemaker, step into a Godfather scene, meet a photographer who lived in a bank, hunt for angels, pass Basquiat’s studio, and finish where Hamilton began. Every stop is outdoors; indoor visits are optional.',legs:['Begin at the Puck Building, at Houston and Lafayette Streets. Find the gilded Puck at the Houston and Mulberry corner.','Walk east on Houston Street to Mott Street, then turn right. The cathedral entrance is on Mott, between Houston and Prince.','Continue south on Mott to Prince Street, go east to Elizabeth Street, then south on Elizabeth to Spring Street. Turn left and walk to the Bowery.','Walk north on the Bowery to Bleecker Street, then west on Bleecker past Lafayette to the top of Crosby Street.','Head back east on Bleecker to Lafayette, walk north to Great Jones Street, and turn right. Number 57 is on your right.','Walk back to Lafayette Street and turn right. Continue north about two blocks; the Public is on your right.']}
